{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>His strength shall be hungry</b> — like <i>ben oni</i> (son of my strength). The meaning is that he will be sated from it." "<b>to his side</b> — like <i>velatzela hamishkan</i> (and to the side of the tabernacle)."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "Reading ישבע as 'he will be sated'; the referent of 'from it' is cryptic in the original."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:02:57.161106341Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}